{"term":"permit","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:398ea99dfb8f16be81","definition":"To allow (something) to happen, to give permission for.","example":"Mr. Cooke at once began a tirade against the residents of Asquith for permitting a sandy and generally disgraceful condition of the roads. So roundly did he vituperate the inn management in particular, and with such a loud flow of words, that I trembled lest he should be heard on the veranda.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["permitable","permit nature to take her course","permittable","permittance","permitter","repermit"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/permit#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:4db3737430b5bc3c15","definition":"To allow (someone) to do something; to give permission to.","example":"He was ultimately cleared, but during that period, Mr. Ackman said, his lawyers would not permit him to defend himself publicly.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["permitable","permit nature to take her course","permittable","permittance","permitter","repermit"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/permit#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e731e8c3ef8f58a33b","definition":"To allow for, to make something possible.","example":"What was left to say? Quite a lot, if only parliamentary time permitted.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["permitable","permit nature to take her course","permittable","permittance","permitter","repermit"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/permit#English",